<h1>Toddler and preschool dance in the La Crosse area</h1>
<h2 class="mt-4">A first introduction to dance</h2>
<p>A young child’s first dance experience is also an introduction to a new room, a teacher, and other children. Misty’s Dance Unlimited offers early childhood dance options for Onalaska, Holmen, and La Crosse area families. Begin with the youngest age groups in our <a href="/fall">class schedule</a> and let us help you find an appropriate starting point.</p>
<h2 class="mt-4">Find a class that fits this stage</h2>
<p>Toddlers and preschoolers can differ greatly in their readiness for a group activity. Share your child’s age and any previous class experience with our team. Ask whether a parent participates in the class you are considering and how the teacher handles arrival and transitions. Do not assume the same format applies to every early childhood class.</p>
<h2 class="mt-4">Make the first visit feel familiar</h2>
<p>Before the lesson, confirm the campus and arrival instructions. Tell your child they will meet a teacher and explore movement with music. Ask what to wear for a trial before buying shoes or a uniform, and bring any questions about your child’s comfort in a new setting. Our team can talk through which class may be a good fit.</p>
<h2 class="mt-4">Plan for your whole family</h2>
<p>For siblings at different ages, compare days and locations rather than selecting a class by its name alone. A Holmen option may suit one family’s week while an Onalaska class suits another. If you want to explore another season, see <a href="/summer">summer classes and camps</a>. When it is time for a celebration, our <a href="/parties">birthday party page</a> explains the available packages and how to inquire.</p>
<h2>Early childhood programs in the 2026–2027 guide</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Mini &amp; Me:</strong> a caretaker-and-child class for 2-year-olds.</li>
<li><strong>Tippy Toes:</strong> an imaginative introduction to ballet for 3-year-olds.</li>
<li><strong>Tutus &amp; Bowties:</strong> basic ballet with storytelling for 4-year-olds.</li>
<li><strong>Fairytale Ballet:</strong> a ballet option for ages 3–4 built around make-believe.</li>
<li><strong>Tiny Tappers:</strong> a rhythm and tap introduction for ages 3–4.</li>
</ul>
<p>Compare the days and campus listings in the <a href="/fall">program guide</a> to find the option that fits your family.</p>
